  "summary": "Malicious code in node-config-svg-contract (npm)",
  "details": "Node-config-svg-contract@1.0.0 exports functions (getPlugin, setPlugin, getPluginExten) that fetch remote content from the non-standard host rest-icon-handler[.]store (URLs hxxps://rest-icon-handler[.]store/icons/103 and /icons/389) and execute it via eval(JSON.parse(body)) with automatic retry. Any consumer that calls one of these exported functions downloads and runs arbitrary remote code from the.store host. A separate exported function (setDefaultModule) fetches from legitimate CDN hosts (cdnjs[.]cloudflare[.]com, fastly[.]net, akamai[.]net, cloudfront[.]net) and appears to be a benign facade masking the remote-code loader.",
